From c1093d545dc0fdd7b590cfcfb3f2d68623f8fd60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:31:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rsz: early sizing takes a top-level port's flat net
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

performEarlySizingRound gets a driver's net with network->net(term) for a
top-level port, and in a hierarchical netlist that is the top module's
dbModNet. performGainBuffering hands it to insertBufferBeforeLoads, whose
staToDb(const Net*) asserts the net is a dbNet (a release build dereferences
the dbModNet as one and takes signal 11). The comment above the line already
says the flat net is wanted; flatNet(term) is it. The trigger is a top-level
input port with more than max_fanout loads in a design that keeps a module:
remove_buffers then repair_design -pre_placement, or a synthesis that builds
no buffers.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 src/rsz/src/RepairDesign.cc | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rsz/src/RepairDesign.cc b/src/rsz/src/RepairDesign.cc
index daff7da..a8ad9dd 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/RepairDesign.cc
+++ b/src/rsz/src/RepairDesign.cc
@@ -169,10 +169,14 @@ void RepairDesign::performEarlySizingRound(int& repaired_net_count)
                2,
                "Processing driver {}",
                network_->pathName(drvr_pin));
-    // Always get the flat net for the top level port.
-    sta::Net* net = network_->isTopLevelPort(drvr_pin)
-                        ? network_->net(network_->term(drvr_pin))
-                        : db_network_->dbToSta(db_network_->flatNet(drvr_pin));
+    // Always get the flat net for the top level port: in a hierarchical
+    // netlist the port's term net is the top module's dbModNet, which
+    // gain buffering cannot insert buffers on.
+    sta::Net* net
+        = network_->isTopLevelPort(drvr_pin)
+              ? db_network_->dbToSta(
+                    db_network_->flatNet(network_->term(drvr_pin)))
+              : db_network_->dbToSta(db_network_->flatNet(drvr_pin));
     if (!net) {
       continue;
     }
